{% from "entrycard.njk" import card %}
<section class="home-intro">
  <span class="eyebrow">Notes on getting it wrong, carefully</span>
  <h1>I build things across borders, then write down what the data alone couldn&rsquo;t tell me.</h1>
  <div class="intro-copy">
    <figure class="intro-portrait">
      <img src="/images/portrait.jpg" alt="Portrait of Sarath Chandra Yanamandra" width="900" height="1125">
      <figcaption>Look Google made a cool photo of me.</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <div>
      <p>Hi, I&rsquo;m Sarath. I do content at KukuFM, and pay attention to how AI, marketing, media, and the operational calls underneath them behave once the presentation ends. I&rsquo;m wrong a fair amount. The writing is how I narrow the error bars.</p>
      <a href="/about/" class="text-link">More about me <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section-block">
  <div class="section-heading">
    <span class="eyebrow">Recently published</span>
    <a href="/writing/" class="text-link">All writing <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></a>
  </div>
  <div class="essay-list">
    {% for post in collections.posts | reverse | head(4) %}{{ card(post) }}{% endfor %}
  </div>
</section>

<section class="project-strip">
  <div class="strip-head">
    <span class="eyebrow">On the workbench</span>
    <h2>Projects and practical studies.</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="project-preview">
    {% for p in projects | head(2) %}
    <a class="proj-teaser" href="/projects/"><span>{{ p.kicker[0] }}</span><h3>{{ p.title }}</h3></a>
    {% endfor %}
    <a href="/projects/" class="text-link">See projects <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></a>
  </div>
</section>
